    "insights": [
      "Generalized Cassini: Gₙ₊₁²−Gₙ₊₁Gₙ−Gₙ² = (−1)ⁿ(b²−ab−a²); the quadratic negates under the recurrence so it is (−1)ⁿ times the fixed discriminant D. Fibonacci D=1, Lucas D=−5.",
      "Weighted sum closed form: 2∑ k GₖGₖ₊₁ = 2n Gₙ₊₁²−2GₙGₙ₊₁+2ab+D·(if Even n then −n else n+1). Induction step = 2(n+1)·Cassini, the SAME certificate as the Fibonacci-only parent.",
      "Parameterizing by (a,b) is free in the proof; only the closed form gains 2ab (n=0 boundary, =0 for Fibonacci) and the D factor on the parity correction."
    ],
    "mathlibGaps": [
      "Mathlib has no general Gibonacci/Horadam sequence or its Cassini/weighted-sum identities; only Nat.fib and (in-repo) lucasU."
    ],
